.git
.claude
.vscode
**/target
**/.mvn
*.log

# The build context is this whole directory (compose.yaml sets `context: ../..`) and the Dockerfile
# does `COPY . .`, so anything here lands in the build stage's layer. The final image is multi-stage
# and takes only the jar, so the published image stays clean -- but the build stage persists in the
# local layer cache on the VPS, and one `--target build` or one cache export would push it.
#
# .env is every secret in the system. backups/ is every student's name, address and ticket history,
# and including it also grows the build context by the whole backup directory on every deploy, on a
# 60 GB disk. Neither has any business in an image.
infra/production/.env
infra/production/.env.*
infra/production/backups/
infra/production/.state/
infra/production/inventory/
